How to use the python script for plotting EEM 

No installation needed.
The data are shown raw, with no scatter filtering: first-order Rayleigh scattering (Em = Ex) and the second-order harmonic (Em = 2·Ex) are left in the maps.

Quick start:
  1. Open Google Colab.
  2. In Colab, select a new file and paste the "Python_Script".
  3. Choose Run all.
  4. Select a file from your computer and upload it.
  4. On the left you will have the full colour scale (logarithmic by default), so the scatter and the weak signal are both visible. On the right: "zoom" scale, with the colours stretched onto the weak signal (the scatter saturates).
  6. Use the Download buttons under the plot to save the normal or zoom version as a PNG (300 dpi).
